groom parks on `awaiting-clarification` from `framing`, and the edge's own `frontmatter-update`
hook records `framing` as the status to come back to — a step body never writes `return_to`. The
mutation report lists that write ahead of both script hooks, which is the order the edge declares
them in.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  tracker:
    driver: cli
-- fixtures/cwd/run/index.md --
---
title: "Demo"
status: framing
return_to: null
---

# Demo
-- fixtures/cwd/run/clarifications.md --
# Clarifications

## C1 — retention window — open

**Asked:** 2026-08-14 — intake

**Question:** How long are archives retained?

**Answer:**
-- cmd --
booping playbook-transition groom awaiting-clarification --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
framing → awaiting-clarification
frontmatter: status=awaiting-clarification
frontmatter index.md: return_to=framing
script tracker-comment: ok
script tracker-sync: ok
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
title: "Demo"
status: awaiting-clarification
return_to: framing
---

# Demo
